---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/github';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Running an analysis"
  description="Load frames, parameters, ROI, and compute in Semper."
  path="/manual/analysis"
>
  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 3rem">
    <p class="crumb">
      <a href={withBase('/manual')}>← Manual</a>
    </p>
    <h2>Running an analysis</h2>
    <p class="sub">Wizard steps from loading frames through ROI and parameters.</p>

    <div class="prose">
      <h3>Step 1 — Load frames</h3>
      <p>Tap each dropzone and pick images. <strong>Photos</strong> is the system picker; <strong>Files</strong> is the only route to RAW and DNG.</p>
      <p>
        The strip shows deformed frames with order badges. <strong>Badge order is analysis
        order.</strong> Tap sort to reorder by name, date, or manually. You cannot restore the
        picker&apos;s original order once sorted.
      </p>

      <h3>Step 2 — Settings</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Region of interest</strong> — defaults to the full image. Edit opens the ROI
          editor.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Single</strong> or <strong>Sweep</strong> — Single solves every frame once. Sweep
          solves one frame across a lattice of settings.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Advanced parameters</strong> — subset, step, strain window, kernel.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Then tap <strong>Compute</strong>.</p>

      <h3>While it runs</h3>
      <p>
        Points solved and convergence update live. <strong>Cancel</strong> stops immediately —
        nothing is kept. Keep the app open; there is no resume if Android kills the process.
      </p>
      <p>
        A run stops itself if images decorrelate: two consecutive frames below 50% convergence end
        it. Frames solved before that are kept as a short (not failed) analysis.
      </p>

      <h3>Parameters (single mode)</h3>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Parameter</th>
            <th>Range</th>
            <th>Default / reset</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Subset size</td>
            <td>15–121, odd</td>
            <td>Recommended from your image</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Step size</td>
            <td>1–30</td>
            <td>5</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Strain window</td>
            <td>5–101, odd</td>
            <td>15</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Kernel</td>
            <td>4×4 Bicubic / 6×6 Keys</td>
            <td>4×4 Bicubic</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        Quote the <strong>VSG</strong> (virtual strain gauge), not only the window:
        <code>VSG = (strain window − 1) × step + 1</code> [px]. Full table:
        <a href={withBase('/learn/parameters')}>Parameters</a>.
      </p>

      <h3>Region of interest</h3>
      <p>
        Draw a rect or square, or type X, Y, W, H. <strong>Crop</strong> sets the area to
        correlate; <strong>Erase</strong> punches holes (grips, fiducials). An ROI smaller than the
        subset will not run.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="cta-row" style="margin-top: 1.5rem">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href={withBase('/manual/sweeps-results')}>Next: Sweeps &amp; results</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={withBase('/manual/getting-started')}>Back</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
